Package: shield-monitor
Version: VERSION_PLACEHOLDER
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Zuken <noreply@localhost>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-venv, python3-setuptools, python3-pyside6.qtcore, python3-pyside6.qtgui, python3-pyside6.qtwidgets, python3-reportlab, arp-scan, nmap, tcpdump, nftables, libnotify-bin, polkitd, pkexec
Suggests: shield-packet-collector, python3-pyqtgraph
Recommends: auditd, bpftrace, bpftool, ieee-data, tshark, dnsutils, fonts-dejavu-core
Description: Zuken Shield endpoint and local-network defense platform
 Zuken Shield monitors endpoint processes, file integrity, USB devices, listening
 sockets, services and local-network threats. It provides deterministic risk
 scoring, incident correlation, reversible response, forensic integrity,
 reports, offline log summaries, MITRE-mapped behavioral detection, local
 anomaly baselines, tamper monitoring and a safe defensive assessment lab.
 .
 The live traffic graph needs python3-pyqtgraph, which is suggested rather than
 required: on Ubuntu it pulls in PyQt6 (GPL-3.0) through an alternative
 dependency, and Shield targets Apache-2.0 and does not import PyQt6. Without
 it the graph is unavailable and everything else is unaffected.
 .
 It ships a monitoring agent, a minimal privileged response helper and a PySide6
 desktop UI. The UI runs as a normal user and communicates over authenticated
 local Unix sockets.
 The UI is fully bilingual (English/Vietnamese, switchable at runtime).
